  <div class="hero" style="height:8px"></div>
  <p><img src="https://substackcdn.example.test/image/fetch/w_1100/jugs.jpeg" width="550" alt="Milk jugs lined up on snow" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;"></p>
  <p>Here is the method I use every January. Cut the jug around its middle, leave a hinge, poke drain holes, and fill it with four inches of damp mix.</p>
  <p>The cold does the work: seeds that need stratification get it for free, and seedlings come up hardened.</p>
  <blockquote style="border-left:4px solid #ff6719;padding-left:12px;color:#555;">Patience is the main ingredient.</blockquote>
